WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.300
The two point x integration is a separate desired-state plan and apply

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:04.762
model.

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:09.288
Configure its own checkout path, executable and reference.

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:14.000
Keep Workflows and Scripts one point x on their compatible legacy

00:00:14.012 --> 00:00:14.575
runtime.

00:00:14.975 --> 00:00:18.000
Runtime recognition only identifies a layout.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:22.712
It does not prove that a target provider, resource schema or mutation

00:00:22.725 --> 00:00:24.175
is supported for your environment.

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:30.000
Open Workflows two point x under Optional Integrations and select

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.000
the intended starter.

00:00:31.388 --> 00:00:35.625
Review the input document, editable global configuration and unique

00:00:35.638 --> 00:00:36.562
state filename.

00:00:36.938 --> 00:00:40.138
Match the installed resource schema and target scope.

00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:42.750
A template selection is not approval.

00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:47.788
Keep state and reviewed inputs associated so later guarded actions

00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:51.375
cannot silently target a different plan or environment.

00:00:52.546 --> 00:00:56.458
Scripts two point x contains converted intent starters.

00:00:56.846 --> 00:01:00.396
They do not execute as the legacy main script command.

00:01:00.808 --> 00:01:04.508
Generate the input and review the corresponding plan in the separate

00:01:04.508 --> 00:01:05.021
runtime.

00:01:05.421 --> 00:01:10.521
P E-only, controller, Foundation and other unmapped legacy actions

00:01:10.533 --> 00:01:12.483
remain in Scripts one point x.

00:01:12.883 --> 00:01:17.483
Do not infer feature parity from similar names across both catalogues.

00:01:18.683 --> 00:01:22.908
Submit the plan through the preview workspace and inspect its durable

00:01:22.921 --> 00:01:24.808
job and retained evidence.

00:01:25.208 --> 00:01:29.608
Confirm the target, resource changes, state and supported provider

00:01:29.608 --> 00:01:30.133
behavior.

00:01:30.521 --> 00:01:34.533
Resolve schema errors and unknowns before considering apply.

00:01:34.933 --> 00:01:39.208
A successful plan does not itself perform or authorize the target

00:01:39.221 --> 00:01:39.708
change.

00:01:40.121 --> 00:01:43.471
Preserve the exact source and input used to produce it.

00:01:44.642 --> 00:01:48.492
Apply and destroy remain distinct approval-bound actions where the

00:01:48.504 --> 00:01:50.154
guarded lane is enabled.

00:01:50.529 --> 00:01:54.392
Review the exact request and use an authorized environment with a

00:01:54.392 --> 00:01:55.429
recovery path.

00:01:55.817 --> 00:01:59.892
Do not bypass approval or use legacy launchers as a workaround.

00:02:00.292 --> 00:02:02.804
Independently read back the target result.

00:02:03.192 --> 00:02:07.604
Preview status and passing software tests do not establish vendor

00:02:07.604 --> 00:02:10.729
support or compatibility for every resource.
